```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: VLM serving system developers (vLLM, SGLang, TensorRT-LLM) and ML platform teams designing scheduling policies who might consider input/prefill-token count as an SJF proxy. Actionable guidance: input-length-SJF causes 1.4-5.8x p99 latency regression vs FCFS at realistic VLM tau (0.14-0.34) and load (rho 0.7-0.95), so use FCFS or a modality-aware/output-length predictor instead.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Sim shows large regressions (1.4x@rho0.7 to 5.8x@rho0.95), but evidence is L0 sim-only (M/G/1, not continuous batching). Packet explicitly states "single-server M/G/1-flavored sim (not true continuous batching); L1 must replay a real vLLM/SGLang VLM trace". Without L1 validation, operational significance is unproven—could be microbenchmark artifact. If L1 confirms, the win is avoiding a catastrophic scheduler misconfiguration.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [L0 sim-only, no real-system validation (packet requires L1 trace replay); No citation in packet that production systems currently deploy input-length-SJF (policy described as hypothetical "cheapest observable"); FCFS is already default in vLLM/SGLang, so result is defensive (avoid bad opt) not an improvement; Capturing SJF benefit requires building accurate output-length predictor, which is non-trivial engineering]
RATIONALE: Packet L0 RESULTS verify SJF p99/FCFS p99 ratio 1.42-5.37x at tau 0.14 (realistic VLM band) across rho 0.7-0.95, with crossover tau* 0.43-0.8 >> realistic tau. Controls pass: C1 oracle SJF beats FCFS (0.72-0.96x), C2 FCFS tau-invariant. However, packet's "What L1 should measure" explicitly requires real vLLM/SGLang trace to "measure the ACTUAL Kendall-tau(input_tokens, realized decode_length) per request" and "confirm measured tau < simulated tau* AND SJF p99 regresses". The realistic tau~0 premise (image-tokens anti-correlate with decode length) is assumed, not measured. No production deployment of input-length-SJF is cited; without L1, the large sim effect may not survive continuous-batching dynamics, paged attention, or prefill/decode disaggregation in real systems.
```
